<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Transylvania</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Transylvania is a historical region in the Carpathian basin, now part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a>. It was an autonomous principality under Ottoman suzerainty in the sixteenth and seventeenth centuries, intervening in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-deluge">Deluge</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-karlowitz">Treaty of Karlowitz</a> of 1699 transferred it to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a>, and it later formed part of the largely rural economy of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/transylvania.jpg" alt="Transylvania" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: BlinxTheKitty · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Transylvania_(Local_2-3).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
